## Primary documentation

The [official distribution](https://www.dhondt.de/) identifies 2.23 as the
available solver. The [2.23 manual](https://www.dhondt.de/ccx_2.23.pdf)
identifies its date as 19 October 2025. Its relevant rules are:

- Shared beam nodes provide stiff connections. Different normals, sections,
  dimensions or offsets can create automatic knots; internal hinges need
  doubled nodes and MPCs (§6.2.33, pp121–124).
- Static prescribed rotations use mean-rotation equations. Older general
  program-structure wording about rotation-triggered knots needs checking
  against the actual implementation (§6.2.33; §10.3.5–8, pp695–698).
- Beam section-force output replaces ordinary stress slots with local forces
  and moments. Original-node output averages expanded quantities, so it is
  insufficient to identify distinct incident element ends (§6.2.33).
- SPRING1 acts in one declared direction; SPRING2 couples declared nodal
  directions. Their scalar laws do not establish a six-component joint
  (§6.2.40–42, pp128–130).
- Beam/shell member nodes cannot belong to an explicit Rigid Body receiving
  set (§7.113, pp589–590).

